From: "claude[bot]" <41898282+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:35:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] T1 font encoding with Latin Modern so accented author
 names extract and copy as single characters
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Referee 4 (minor 13) reported mangled names. The glyph-to-Unicode maps fixed
the ligatures (Griffiths, Jeffrey), but under OT1 accented letters were still
built from a separate accent glyph and extracted as '¨Ozkan', 'ˇSoˇsi´c',
'L´ala'. With T1 and Latin Modern they extract as Özkan, Šošić and Lála.
Pagination is unchanged.
---
 main.tex | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main.tex b/main.tex
index ccea161..7cfcb63 100644
--- a/main.tex
+++ b/main.tex
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@
 % \usepackage[margin=1.5cm]{geometry} 
 \usepackage[english]{babel}
 \usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
+\usepackage[T1]{fontenc} % accented names (\"O, \v{S}, \'a) as single glyphs, so they extract and copy correctly
+\usepackage{lmodern}
 \usepackage[]{graphicx}
 \usepackage{xspace}
 \usepackage{siunitx}
-- 
